steiner@math.bgsu.edu wrote:
> Hello, all!
>      I'm a newcomer to Nethack and I have a couple of questions:
> 1). How does one acquire teleportation power in the game?
> Does eating a certain corpse do the trick?

You can acquire what's called the "teleportation intrinsic" by eating a
number of corpses (hint: you are what you eat, so if a certain being
can teleport, chances are you'll be able to too after you eat its
corpse.)

Of course, you're not guaranteed to like it once you do...(More
specifically, teleportation isn't much good unless you have some means
of controlling either a) when you teleport, b) where you go, or c)
both.)

There's a variety of other ways you can teleport -- namely, certain
objects confer this power (some only once, others indefinitely...)
There is also a particular class which gains this power at a given
experience level.

> 2). I can play the first 4 levels quite well, but
> every time I get to level 5 a killer bee gets me.
> What is the best way to fight a killer bee?

1. Have poison resistance.
2. Be fast if possible (i.e. NOT burdened)
3. Down a hallway (so you're only fighting one at a time).
4. From a distance if possible (though the little suckers are horribly
tough to hit.)
5. Elbereth if all else fails...

